 "intro_html": "Yomogi daifuku, also called kusa daifuku (\"grass daifuku\"), is the spring version of <a href=\"daifuku.html\">daifuku</a>: the mochi is coloured and scented with yomogi, Japanese mugwort. Dried yomogi powder makes it possible any time of year. It tastes green and slightly bitter, like fresh herbs, which suits chunky tsubuan <a href=\"anko.html\">anko</a> best. A little powder colours a lot, so measure it.",
