 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Roll the anko into <b>6 balls of <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"30\" data-s=\"0\">30 g</span></b> and set them on a plate in the fridge.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Roll the anko",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Roll each ball between your palms.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/1-how1.webp?v=2730142f05"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/1.webp?v=739d4d1ac8",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>5 min</span>",
   "title": "Roll the anko",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"180\">180 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Anko (red bean paste)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Stir the <b>yomogi powder</b> with the <b>hot water</b> into a thick, dark green paste.</li><li>Leave it <b>5 minutes</b>. The powder softens and the grassy smell comes up.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wake up the yomogi",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Stir the powder with a tablespoon of hot water into a thick paste.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/2-how1.webp?v=1ec529c370"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/2.webp?v=c0eefa14ed",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>5 min</span>",
   "title": "Wake up the yomogi",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"5\">5 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Yomogi (mugwort) powder"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Hot water"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>In a heatproof glass bowl, stir the <b>shiratamako</b> and <b>sugar</b> together.</li><li>Add the <b>water</b> a little at a time, stirring and pressing out the lumps, until it's smooth and pours like thick cream.</li><li>Stir in the <b>yomogi paste</b> until the batter is one even green, with no dark streaks.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Mix the batter",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Add the water a little at a time and press out the lumps.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/3-how1.webp?v=f084b95496"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Stir in the yomogi paste until the batter is one even green.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/3-how2.webp?v=e4859aed2b"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/3.webp?v=00610afa11",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>3 min</span>",
   "title": "Mix the batter",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"100\">100 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Shiratamako (glutinous rice flour)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"25\">25 g</span>",
     "name_html": "White sugar"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"120\">120 ml</span>",
     "name_html": "Water"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cover loosely with cling film. Microwave <b>1 minute</b> at 600–700 W, then stir hard with a wet spatula. The edges will have set first.</li><li>Another <b>1 minute</b>, stir again. It's now a sticky lump.</li><li>Another <b>20–30 seconds</b>, until the whole mass is <b>translucent</b>, glossy and stretchy, deep green with no pale, opaque patches. Stir once more.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Microwave in three bursts",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "1 minute, then stir hard with a wet spatula: the edges set first.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/4-how1.webp?v=46893cfcf7"
     },
     {
      "caption": "After the last burst it's translucent and stretchy all through.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/4-how2.webp?v=942d951d69"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/4.webp?v=a835bd4316",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Microwave in three bursts",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Sift a thick layer of <b>potato starch</b> over a tray. Scrape the hot mochi onto it and dust the top too.</li><li>With a dusted bench scraper, cut it into <b>6 even pieces</b>, about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"40\" data-s=\"0\">40 g</span> each. Wait a minute or two, until you can handle it.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Divide on starch",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Cut into six with a dusted bench scraper.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/5-how1.webp?v=b34b66969f"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/5.webp?v=e2717bfcab",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>5 min</span>",
   "title": "Divide on starch",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"3\">3 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Potato starch (katakuriko)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Take one piece and stretch it into a disc about <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"8\" data-s=\"0\">8 cm</span></b> across with starchy fingers. Make the edge a little thinner than the middle.</li><li>Set an anko ball in the middle.</li><li>Pull the edge up over the ball in four or five pleats and <b>pinch them together</b> on top. Twist off any extra.</li><li>Turn it over so the seam is underneath, and cup it in your palm to round it.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wrap and pinch shut",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Stretch a piece into an 8 cm disc, edge thinner than the middle.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/6-how1.webp?v=8f34c1fdb2"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Anko ball in the middle; pleat the edge up over it and pinch shut.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/6-how2.webp?v=b0eb723038"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/6.webp?v=7dddf5af5c",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 6,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>10 min</span>",
   "title": "Wrap and pinch shut",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Brush off the loose starch.</li><li>Serve the same day, at room temperature. Cut one in half with a wet knife to show the dark anko inside the green mochi.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-7",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Brush and serve",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Brush off the loose starch; cut with a wet knife to show the inside.",
      "src": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/7-how1.webp?v=05d71d9c74"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yomogi-daifuku/7.webp?v=1adc24ca7d",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 7,
